    "title": "crypto: accept empty HMAC keys",
    "user": {
      "login": "l0rinc",
      "id": 1841944,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1841944?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/l0rinc",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**Problem:** `CHMAC_SHA256` and `CHMAC_SHA512` copied the key with `memcpy(rkey, key, keylen)` before zero-padding it.\r\nEmpty-vector callers can pass a null key pointer, and glibc annotates `memcpy` arguments as non-null.\r\nA minimal [Compiler Explorer reproducer](https://godbolt.org/z/jMPP8EhEr) shows the unguarded zero-length copy still aborting under current GCC-trunk UBSan, while the guarded variant exits successfully.\r\nThis is the same class of empty-byte-vector issue [discussed for the IPC fuzzer](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35118#discussion_r3508842395) - where `std::copy` was also considered (see godbolt reproducer above).\r\n\r\nNo in-tree caller currently passes a null HMAC key, so this hardens the empty-key boundary for tests and fuzzing.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Skip the key copy when `keylen == 0`. The following `memset` still zero-fills the whole HMAC key block, so the derived pads and digests are unchanged.\r\n\r\nWith the HMAC copy fixed, the crypto fuzzer can pass empty byte vectors directly.\r\nThe stale `eval_script` workaround can also be dropped in favor of calling `ConsumeRemainingBytes()` directly because it already returns before copying when no bytes remain.\r\n",
